<%#
  One number shown as its share of another: the label and the raw counts on one
  line, the bar under them, and a sentence saying what the proportion means.

  The counts are spelled out beside the bar on purpose -- a bar alone tells a
  reader the shape of the answer but never the number they came for.

  Locals:
    label      - what is being counted
    counts     - the counts in words, e.g. "1,536 of 1,842 expected"
    percentage - 0..100
    variant    - progress bar colour
    caption    - one sentence explaining the proportion (optional)
%>
<div class="mb-4">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-x-4">
    <span class="font-semibold text-heading"><%= label %></span>
    <span><%= counts %></span>
  </div>
  <%= ui_progress_bar percentage, variant, class: "my-1",
                      aria: { label: "#{label}: #{percentage}%" } %>
  <% if local_assigns[:caption].present? %>
    <div class="text-stone-subtle"><%= caption %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
